WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.650
I was invited to a cookout on an old friend’s farm in western Washington.
我应邀去一位老朋友在华盛顿州西部的农场参加野炊。

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:13.090
I parked my car outside the farm and walked past a milking house which had apparently not been used in many years.
我把车停在农场外，走过一间挤奶房，看样子它已经很多年没人用过了。

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:17.360
A noise at a window caught my attention, so I went inside.
窗边传来的一阵响动引起了我的注意，于是我走了进去。

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.130
It was a hummingbird, desperately trying to escape.
原来是一只蜂鸟，正拼命想要逃出去。

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:25.670
She was covered in spider-webs and was barely able to move her wings.
她浑身缠满了蛛网，几乎扇不动翅膀。

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:29.190
She ceased her struggle the instant I picked her up.
我一把她捧起来，她就不再挣扎了。

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:33.860
With the bird in my cupped hand, I looked around to see how she had gotten in.
我把小鸟捧在拢起的手心里，环顾四周，想看看她是怎么进来的。

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:37.210
The broken window glass was the likely answer.
窗户上的玻璃破了，八成就是从那儿进来的。

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:43.390
I stuffed a piece of cloth into the hole and took her outside, closing the door securely behind me.
我把一块布塞进破洞，带着她走到外面，随手把门关严。

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:49.460
When I opened my hand, the bird did not fly away; she sat looking at me with her bright eyes.
我张开手，小鸟却没有飞走；她就那么待着，用明亮的眼睛望着我。

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:53.550
I removed the sticky spider-webs that covered her head and wings.
我把粘在她头上和翅膀上的蛛网一点点摘掉。

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:56.260
Still, she made no attempt to fly.
可她还是一点儿也不想飞。

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:01.010
Perhaps she had been struggling against the window too long and was too tired?
也许她对着窗户挣扎太久，累得没力气了？

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:02.860
Or too thirsty?
还是渴坏了？

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:09.890
As I carried her up the blackberry-lined path toward my car where I kept a water bottle, she began to move.
我捧着她沿着两旁长满黑莓的小路朝车子走去——车里放着一瓶水——这时她开始动了。

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:14.740
I stopped, and she soon took wing but did not immediately fly away.
我停下脚步，她很快就飞了起来，却没有马上飞走。

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:18.350
Hovering, she approached within six inches of my face.
她悬停在空中，飞到离我的脸不到六英寸的地方。

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:24.800
For a very long moment, this tiny creature looked into my eyes, turning her head from side to side.
这个小生灵望着我的眼睛，脑袋左右转动，过了好久好久。

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.270
Then she flew quickly out of sight.
接着，她飞快地飞走，不见了踪影。

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:31.990
During the cookout, I told my hosts about the hummingbird incident.
野炊时，我把蜂鸟这件事讲给主人听。

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:34.400
They promised to fix the window.
他们答应会把窗户修好。

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.400
As I was departing, my friends walked me to my car.
我要走的时候，朋友们送我到车旁。

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:44.320
I was standing by the car when a hummingbird flew to the center of our group and began hovering.
我正站在车边，一只蜂鸟飞到我们这群人中间，开始悬停。

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.080
She turned from person to person until she came to me.
她从一个人面前转到另一个人面前，直到来到我跟前。

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.290
She again looked directly into my eyes, then let out a squeaking call and was gone.
她又一次直视我的眼睛，随后发出一声尖细的鸣叫，便不见了。

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.280
For a moment, all were speechless.
一时间，大家都说不出话来。

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:00.200
Then someone said, “She must have come to say goodbye.”
接着有人说：“她一定是来道别的。”

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.750
A few weeks later, I went to the farm again.
几周后，我又去了那座农场。

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:07.220
I was just about to leave when the hummingbird appeared.
我正要离开，那只蜂鸟出现了。
